1
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Don't look for a reason... Look for a way out.

2
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Cube is a thriller, science fiction, mystery film directed by Vincenzo Natali.

3
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:06,000
A group of strangers find themselves trapped in a maze-like prison.

4
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:06,000
It soon becomes clear that each of them possesses the peculiar skills
necessary to escape, if they don't wind up dead first.

5
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:06,000
Leaven, played by Nicole De Boer.

6
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Holloway, played by Nicky Guadagni.

7
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Quentin, played by Maurice Dean Wint.

8
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Worth, played by David Hewlett.

9
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Kazan, played by Andrew Miller.

10
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Rennes, played by Wayne Robson.

11
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Cube is a 1997 Canadian science fiction horror film
directed and co-written by Vincenzo Natali.

12
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
A product of the Canadian Film Centre's First Feature Project, Nicole de Boer, Nicky Guadagni, David Hewlett, Andrew Miller, Julian Richings,
Wayne Robson, and Maurice Dean Wint star as seven individuals trapped in a bizarre and deadly labyrinth of cube-shaped rooms.

13
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
Cube gained notoriety and a cult following for its surreal and
Kafkaesque setting in industrial, cube-shaped rooms.

14
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
It received generally positive reviews and led to a series of films.

15
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
A Japanese remake was released in 2021.

16
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
The film explores themes of escape, entrapment, riddle, autism, mathematics.

17
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
The tone is mind_bending and thought_provoking and intense.
